| b | 19 |  |  |  |
| d | 23 | 12 |  |  |
| e | 8 | 22 | 26 |  |

@right

Cluster ac contains 2 genes; e contains 1. Their distances to b are 19 and 22.

Is the distance from ace to b 20 or 20.5? Why?

=== layout: one-panel

# Update the Distances

@body

Average the original distances between genes in the two clusters.

- ace to b: (18 + 20 + 22) / 3 = 20
- ace to d: (22 + 24 + 26) / 3 = 24

Weight each gene equally: (2 x 19 + 1 x 22) / 3 = 20. The unweighted cluster average gives 20.5.

